# ⚠️ The build context is the **repository root** (see deploy/Dockerfile), so this file is what keeps a machine's
# state out of the image. Everything excluded here is either installed inside the image or is data that must only
# ever arrive as a mounted volume.
node_modules/
.venv/
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ⚠️ **Machine state, and the reason the exclusion matters is not size.** `store/` is mounted as a volume at run
# time; baking a copy into the image would freeze one machine's history and give the container a `store/` that
# nothing updates. `var/` is where the wrapper's log lands — without it a scheduled run is *completely silent*,
# because the wrapper redirects everything into that file.
#
# ⚠️ **`output/` and `resource/` are no longer listed, and their absence is now structural rather than a rule.**
# They left the repository for the shared data root (see `docs/adr/0007`), so a data root that is outside the
# build context **cannot** be baked into the image even by mistake — which is a stronger guarantee than a line
# here. The brief's data arrives mounted at `/data` (`MARKET_OVERVIEW_DATA`), never copied.
store/
var/
credentials/
.config/

# ⚠️ **The Song Reel is a second product and is never in this image.** It lives at `src/song-video/` — inside the
# very tree the `COPY src ./src` line copies — so without this line the brief's image would ship the reel's Remotion
# program, its committed `store/` and its `pyproject.toml`. The reel is built and run by hand from a checkout
# (ADR 0004); nothing about it belongs in a container whose whole job is one brief a day.
src/song-video/

# Not needed to build. `remotion/fonts/` is **not** excluded — the vendored face is source, not an asset.
docs/
tests/
public/
remotion-out/
.remotion/
